-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Precision:** Tri-linear interpolation and compositing are sensitive to floating-point precision, especially with many samples [S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial].
-*   **Boundaries:** Handling rays that do not intersect the volume or intersect only partially requires careful boundary checks during traversal [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Degenerate Input:** Non-orthogonal sampling grids require specific corrections during data preparation to avoid artifacts [S3, unofficial].
+### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
+*   **Precision:** Tri-linear interpolation and compositing are sensitive to floating-point precision, especially with large dynamic ranges in opacity [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Boundaries:** Interpolation at the edges of the voxel grid requires handling out-of-bounds accesses, typically by clamping or mirroring [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Degenerate Input:** Non-orthogonal sampling grids or missing data require specific correction steps during data preparation [S3, unofficial].
